ssing tests, and feature opportunities while implementing.\n- Codex may implement improvements that fit the approved plan or are required for correctness, validation, safety, or a trustworthy MVP.\n- Codex must record deferred ideas in `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` instead of silently expanding scope.\n- Improvements that materially change scope, architecture, data, cost, risk, or timeline require user approval before implementation.\n## Codex Runtime\n- Model: gpt-5.5\n- Coding reasoning: low\n- Planning/model helper reasoning: gpt-5.5 / low\n- Access: full local access\n- Shell environment: inherited from the local supervisor process\n- Account/config/plugins: same local Codex account and CODEX_HOME configuration used by this machine\n## Proposed Internal Responsibilities\n1. Build static app - Create a new Codexa project named codexa-bench-smoke4-01-quote-board-1780177241 and, after approval, build a tiny browser-only static quote board app with saved favorite quotes using index.html, styles.css, script.js, README.md, local validation, and concise continuous progress updates.. Validation: test -f index.html && test -f styles.css && test -f script.js, node --check script.js, test -f README.md, test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md.\n## Assumptions\n- Favorites persist with browser localStorage.\n- The app is static and can be opened directly from index.html without a dev server.\n- No backend, accounts, database, payments, or deployment are in scope.\n- Seed quotes can be hardcoded locally.\n## Open Questions\n- None recorded yet.\n## Validation Plan\n- test -f index.html && test -f styles.css && test -f script.js\n- node --check script.js\n- test -f README.md\n- test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md\n## Completion Bar\n- Files exist in this repo.\n- Validation commands pass or failures are reported honestly.\n- The final summary is grounded in changed files and commands.\n- No docs-only success.\nGenerated: 2026-05-30T21:42:34.591Z\n","exit_code":0,"statu